Class is a blueprint or template that defines variables and functions in one place.
You create multiple objects from one class — each object gets its own data but shares the same functions.

Object is an instance created from a class — like a real server built from a blueprint.
Each object has its own data (variables) but uses the same functions defined in the class.

self refers to the current object calling the function — it tells Python which object's data to use.
Without self Python cannot distinguish between different objects' variables.

